module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Completeness
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.CompletedConnectionDeRham
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.Cosimplicial.CompletedForms

/-!
# Base change of a module with a completed connection along a divided power morphism

Let `p` be a prime, let `D → D'` be a map of commutative rings, let `Ω` be a `D`-module with a
map `d : D → Ω` and `Ω'` a `D'`-module with a map `d' : D' → Ω'`, and let `ψ : Ω → Ω'` be a map
semilinear over `D → D'` and compatible with the two differentials, `ψ (d x) = d' (x mod D')`.
A module `M` over `D` carrying a completed connection `∇ : M → M ⊗̂_D Ω` base-changes to the
module

`M' = M ⊗̂_{D} D' = AdicCompletion (p) (D' ⊗[D] M)`

over `D'`, with a completed connection `∇' : M' → M' ⊗̂_{D'} Ω'`. This is the completed analogue
of `Crystalline.Connection.baseChange` (Remark [Stacks, Tag 07KJ]), and it is the functor `F` of
the proof of [Stacks, Lemma 60.17.5, Tag 07L5].

The connection `∇'` is the base change of `∇` plus a correction coming from the differential of
the new scalars. On a pure tensor

`∇' (b' ⊗ m) = b' · ψ_*(∇ m) + (1 ⊗ m) ⊗ d' b'`,

where `ψ_*` is `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChangeValues`; equivalently,

`∇' (b' • x) = b' • ∇' x + x ⊗ d' b'`      for `b' : D'` and `x : M'`,

which is the Leibniz rule of [Stacks, Tag 07JC] for `∇'` over `D'`.

Given a graded comparison `ψ_i : Ω^i_D → Ω^i_{D'}`, semilinear over `D → D'`, multiplicative for
the wedge product and commuting with the de Rham differentials of the forms, the degree-`i` maps
`M ⊗̂_D Ω^i_D → M' ⊗̂_{D'} Ω^i_{D'}` assemble into a morphism of the completed de Rham complexes
`M ⊗^∧_D Ω^*_D ⟶ M' ⊗^∧_{D'} Ω^*_{D'}`, the map `α` of the proof of
[Stacks, Lemma 60.21.4, Tag 07LH].

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier`: the base-changed module
  `M' = M ⊗̂_{D} D'`.
* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChangeInclusion`: the semilinear map `m ↦ 1 ⊗ m`.
* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChangeValues`: the map `ψ_*` induced on the values of a
  completed connection.
* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.correction`: the Leibniz correction term `x ⊗ ω`, as a
  `D'`-linear map in `x`.
* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.rawFormula`: the formula
  `(b', m) ↦ b' · ψ_*(∇ m) + (1 ⊗ m) ⊗ d' b'` on the generators.
* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.rawBaseChange`: the base-changed connection on the
  uncompleted `D' ⊗[D] M`.
* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.levelBaseChange`: that connection at the level `pⁿ`.
* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChange`: the base-changed completed connection.
* `Crystalline.Pair.baseChange`: the base-changed pair.
* `Crystalline.CompletedDeRham.baseChangeTerm`: the degree-`i` component
  `M ⊗̂_D Ω^i_D → M' ⊗̂_{D'} Ω^i_{D'}` of the base change map of de Rham complexes.
* `Crystalline.CompletedDeRham.baseChangeComplexHom`: the base change map of completed de Rham
  complexes `M ⊗^∧_D Ω^*_D ⟶ M' ⊗^∧_{D'} Ω^*_{D'}`.

## Main results

* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.isPAdicallyComplete_baseChangeCarrier`: `M'` is `p`-adically
  complete.
* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChange_of_tmul`: the formula
  `∇' (b' ⊗ m) = b' · ψ_*(∇ m) + (1 ⊗ m) ⊗ d' b'`.
* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChange_smul`: the Leibniz rule
  `∇' (b' • x) = b' • ∇' x + x ⊗ d' b'` on the whole of `M'`.
* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChange_inclusion`: `∇' (1 ⊗ m) = ψ_*(∇ m)`.
* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.correction_val_congr`: the correction term depends on a
  module element only through its level-`pⁿ` reduction.
* `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChange_eq_of_val`: a map computed at every level by the
  uncompleted formula is the base-changed connection.
* `Crystalline.CompletedDeRham.baseChangeValues_wedgeMap`: left exterior multiplication commutes
  with the base change of the values of a connection.
* `Crystalline.CompletedDeRham.baseChangeTerm_comm`: the degree-`i` components commute with the
  two de Rham differentials.

## Implementation notes

The formula for `∇'` is biadditive in `(b', m)` and balanced over `D`, so it defines an additive
map `D' ⊗[D] M → M' ⊗̂_{D'} Ω'`. This map is not `D'`-linear; it descends to each level `pⁿ`
because `(p)ⁿ` is generated by the integer `pⁿ` and every additive map is `ℤ`-linear, and the
levels assemble into a map out of the completion. The Leibniz rule extends from the dense image of
`D' ⊗[D] M` to all of `M'` because the kernel of the level-`n` evaluation is exactly `(p)ⁿ · M'`
(`AdicCompletion.pow_smul_top_eq_ker_eval`), as `(p)` is finitely generated.

The map `d'` is assumed additive and to satisfy the product rule
`d' (x * y) = x · d' y + y · d' x`, and `ψ` to satisfy `ψ (d x) = d' (x mod D')`. Of the
conditions of a pair, integrability [Stacks, Tag 07JD], topological quasi-nilpotence
[Stacks, Tag 07JE] and the existence of coordinate operators are hypotheses of
`Crystalline.Pair.baseChange`: they are stated in the coordinates `d x_i` of `Ω`, and
`ψ (d x_i)` need not be a coordinate family for `Ω'`.

The de Rham comparison fixes one universe for `D`, `D'`, the two families of forms and `M`, since
`Crystalline.CompletedDeRham.complex` lands in `AddCommGrpCat.{max v w}`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07KJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07KJ)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 60.17.5, Tag 07L5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07L5)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 60.21.4, Tag 07LH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07LH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JE)
-/

@[expose] public section

open DividedPowers
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u u' v v' w uI uI'

namespace Crystalline

namespace CompletedConnection

section BaseChange

variable (p : ℕ) (D : Type u) [CommRing D] (D' : Type u') [CommRing D'] [Algebra D D']

/-! ### The `p`-adic ideals of the two rings -/

/-- The ideal `(p)` of a commutative ring is finitely generated: it is generated by one element. -/
public theorem pAdicIdeal_fg : (pAdicIdeal (A := D) p).FG :=
  Submodule.fg_span_singleton _

/-- The ideal `(p) ⊆ D` maps onto the ideal `(p) ⊆ D'`, both being generated by the image of the
integer `p`. -/
public theorem pAdicIdeal_map_eq :
    (pAdicIdeal (A := D) p).map (algebraMap D D') = pAdicIdeal (A := D') p := by
  rw [pAdicIdeal, pAdicIdeal, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, map_natCast]

/-- The ideal `(p) ⊆ D` maps into the ideal `(p) ⊆ D'`. -/
public theorem pAdicIdeal_map_le :
    (pAdicIdeal (A := D) p).map (algebraMap D D') ≤ pAdicIdeal (A := D') p :=
  le_of_eq (pAdicIdeal_map_eq p D D')

/-! ### The base-changed module -/

variable (M : Type w) [AddCommGroup M] [Module D M]

/-- **The base-changed module `M' = M ⊗̂_{D} D'`**: the `p`-adic completion of `D' ⊗[D] M`, as a
`D'`-module. -/
public abbrev baseChangeCarrier : Type (max u' w) :=
  AdicCompletion (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) (D' ⊗[D] M)

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 07JB] for the base-changed module**: `M'` is `p`-adically complete, being an
adic completion along the finitely generated ideal `(p)`. -/
public theorem isPAdicallyComplete_baseChangeCarrier :
    IsPAdicallyComplete p D' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :=
  AdicCompletion.isAdicComplete (pAdicIdeal_fg p D')

/-- The semilinear inclusion `m ↦ 1 ⊗ m` of `M` into the base-changed module. -/
public noncomputable def baseChangeInclusion :
    M →ₛₗ[algebraMap D D'] baseChangeCarrier p D D' M where
  toFun m := AdicCompletion.of (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) (D' ⊗[D] M) ((1 : D') ⊗ₜ[D] m)
  map_add' m n := by rw [TensorProduct.tmul_add, _root_.map_add]
  map_smul' c m := by
    rw [← map_smul]
    congr 1
    rw [← TensorProduct.smul_tmul, TensorProduct.smul_tmul']
    congr 1
    rw [Algebra.smul_def, smul_eq_mul]

/-- The semilinear inclusion, as a formula. -/
public theorem baseChangeInclusion_apply (m : M) :
    baseChangeInclusion p D D' M m =
      AdicCompletion.of (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) (D' ⊗[D] M) ((1 : D') ⊗ₜ[D] m) :=
  rfl

/-- The image of `b' ⊗ m` in the completion is `b'` times the image of `1 ⊗ m`. -/
public theorem of_tmul_eq_smul_inclusion (b' : D') (m : M) :
    AdicCompletion.of (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) (D' ⊗[D] M) (b' ⊗ₜ[D] m) =
      b' • baseChangeInclusion p D D' M m := by
  rw [baseChangeInclusion_apply, ← map_smul]
  congr 1
  rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul', smul_eq_mul, mul_one]

/-! ### The map induced on the values of a completed connection -/

variable (Omega : Type v) [AddCommGroup Omega] [Module D Omega]
  (Omega' : Type v') [AddCommGroup Omega'] [Module D' Omega']
  (d' : D' → Omega') (psi : Omega →ₛₗ[algebraMap D D'] Omega')

/-- The semilinear map `M ⊗_D Ω → M' ⊗_{D'} Ω'` on the uncompleted tensor products, applying
`m ↦ 1 ⊗ m` to the first factor and `ψ` to the second. -/
public noncomputable def baseChangeTensor :
    (M ⊗[D] Omega) →ₛₗ[algebraMap D D'] (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M ⊗[D'] Omega') :=
  TensorProduct.map (baseChangeInclusion p D D' M) psi

/-- **The map `ψ_*` induced on the values of a completed connection**, `M ⊗̂_D Ω → M' ⊗̂_{D'} Ω'`.
It is the completion of `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChangeTensor`, the two completions
being taken along `(p) ⊆ D` and `(p) ⊆ D'`. -/
public noncomputable def baseChangeValues :
    CompletedTensor p D Omega M →ₛₗ[algebraMap D D']
      CompletedTensor p D' Omega' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :=
  adicCompletionMapₛₗ (baseChangeTensor p D D' M Omega Omega' psi) (pAdicIdeal_map_le p D D')

/-- `ψ_*` on the image of an uncompleted pure tensor. -/
public theorem baseChangeValues_of_tmul (m : M) (omega : Omega) :
    baseChangeValues p D D' M Omega Omega' psi
        (toCompletedTensor p D Omega M (m ⊗ₜ[D] omega)) =
      toCompletedTensor p D' Omega' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M)
        (baseChangeInclusion p D D' M m ⊗ₜ[D'] psi omega) := by
  rw [baseChangeValues, adicCompletionMapₛₗ_of]
  rfl

/-! ### The Leibniz correction term -/

/-- **The Leibniz correction term `x ⊗ ω`** of the base-changed connection, read as a `D'`-linear
map in `x` for a fixed one-form `ω`. -/
public noncomputable def correction (omega : Omega') :
    baseChangeCarrier p D D' M →ₗ[D']
      CompletedTensor p D' Omega' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :=
  (toCompletedTensor p D' Omega' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M)).comp
    ((TensorProduct.mk D' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) Omega').flip omega)

/-- The correction term, as a formula: it is the image of `x ⊗ ω` in the completion. -/
public theorem correction_apply (omega : Omega') (x : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :
    correction p D D' M Omega' omega x =
      toCompletedTensor p D' Omega' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) (x ⊗ₜ[D'] omega) :=
  rfl

/-- A scalar may be moved from the form to the module argument of the correction term. -/
public theorem correction_smul_form (b' : D') (omega : Omega')
    (x : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :
    correction p D D' M Omega' (b' • omega) x =
      correction p D D' M Omega' omega (b' • x) := by
  rw [correction_apply, correction_apply, TensorProduct.smul_tmul]

/-- The correction term is additive in the form. -/
public theorem correction_add_form (omega eta : Omega') (x : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :
    correction p D D' M Omega' (omega + eta) x =
      correction p D D' M Omega' omega x + correction p D D' M Omega' eta x := by
  rw [correction_apply, correction_apply, correction_apply, TensorProduct.tmul_add,
    _root_.map_add]

/-- A `D'`-linear map carries `(p)ⁿ · X` into `(p)ⁿ · Y`. -/
public theorem map_mem_pow_smul_top {X : Type*} [AddCommGroup X] [Module D' X]
    {Y : Type*} [AddCommGroup Y] [Module D' Y] (f : X →ₗ[D'] Y) (n : ℕ) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∈ ((pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) ^ n • ⊤ : Submodule D' X)) :
    f x ∈ ((pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) ^ n • ⊤ : Submodule D' Y) := by
  exact Submodule.smul_top_le_comap_smul_top _ f hx

/-- A pure tensor whose left factor lies in the kernel of the level-`n` evaluation lies in
`(p)ⁿ` times the tensor product. -/
public theorem tmul_mem_pow_smul_top_of_val_eq_zero (n : ℕ) {y : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M}
    (hy : y.val n = 0) (omega : Omega') :
    y ⊗ₜ[D'] omega ∈
      ((pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) ^ n • ⊤ :
        Submodule D' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M ⊗[D'] Omega')) := by
  have hmem : y ∈ ((pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) ^ n • ⊤ :
      Submodule D' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M)) := by
    rw [AdicCompletion.pow_smul_top_eq_ker_eval (pAdicIdeal_fg p D')]
    simpa [AdicCompletion.eval_apply] using hy
  exact map_mem_pow_smul_top p D'
    ((TensorProduct.mk D' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) Omega').flip omega) n hmem

/-- The correction term depends on a module element only through its level-`n` reduction. -/
public theorem correction_val_congr (n : ℕ) (omega : Omega')
    {x y : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M} (h : x.val n = y.val n) :
    (correction p D D' M Omega' omega x).val n =
      (correction p D D' M Omega' omega y).val n := by
  have hz : (x - y).val n = 0 := by rw [AdicCompletion.val_sub_apply, h, sub_self]
  rw [← sub_eq_zero, ← AdicCompletion.val_sub_apply, ← map_sub, correction_apply,
    AdicCompletion.of_apply, Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
  exact tmul_mem_pow_smul_top_of_val_eq_zero p D D' M Omega' n hz omega

/-! ### The base-changed connection on the uncompleted tensor product -/

variable {d : D → Omega} (nabla : CompletedConnection p D Omega d M)

/-- A map satisfying the product rule kills `1`. -/
public theorem eq_zero_of_leibniz {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N]
    [Module R N] {dd : R → N} (hleib : ∀ x y : R, dd (x * y) = x • dd y + y • dd x) :
    dd 1 = 0 := by
  have h : dd 1 + dd 1 = dd 1 + 0 := by
    rw [add_zero]
    have h1 := hleib 1 1
    rw [mul_one, one_smul] at h1
    exact h1.symm
  exact add_left_cancel h

/-- **The defining formula of the base-changed connection** on the generators of `D' ⊗[D] M`:
`(b', m) ↦ b' · ψ_*(∇ m) + (1 ⊗ m) ⊗ d' b'`. -/
public noncomputable def rawFormula (b' : D') (m : M) :
    CompletedTensor p D' Omega' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :=
  b' • baseChangeValues p D D' M Omega Omega' psi (nabla m) +
    correction p D D' M Omega' (d' b') (baseChangeInclusion p D D' M m)

/-- The defining formula is additive in the module argument. -/
public theorem rawFormula_add_right (b' : D') (m n : M) :
    rawFormula p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla b' (m + n) =
      rawFormula p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla b' m +
        rawFormula p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla b' n := by
  rw [rawFormula, rawFormula, rawFormula, nabla.map_add]
  simp only [_root_.map_add, smul_add]
  abel

/-- The defining formula is additive in the scalar argument, given that `d'` is additive. -/
public theorem rawFormula_add_left (hadd' : ∀ x y : D', d' (x + y) = d' x + d' y)
    (b c : D') (m : M) :
    rawFormula p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla (b + c) m =
      rawFormula p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla b m +
        rawFormula p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla c m := by
  rw [rawFormula, rawFormula, rawFormula, hadd' b c, add_smul, correction_add_form]
  abel

/-- **The defining formula is balanced over `D`**, given the Leibniz rule for `∇`, the product
rule for `d'` and the compatibility `ψ (d c) = d' (c mod D')`. -/
public theorem rawFormula_balanced
    (hleib' : ∀ x y : D', d' (x * y) = x • d' y + y • d' x)
    (hpsi : ∀ x : D, psi (d x) = d' (algebraMap D D' x)) (c : D) (b' : D') (m : M) :
    rawFormula p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla (c • b') m =
      rawFormula p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla b' (c • m) := by
  have hform : d' (c • b') =
      algebraMap D D' c • d' b' + b' • d' (algebraMap D D' c) := by
    rw [Algebra.smul_def, hleib']
  have hnabla : baseChangeValues p D D' M Omega Omega' psi (nabla (c • m)) =
      algebraMap D D' c • baseChangeValues p D D' M Omega Omega' psi (nabla m) +
        correction p D D' M Omega' (d' (algebraMap D D' c))
          (baseChangeInclusion p D D' M m) := by
    rw [nabla.leibniz, _root_.map_add, map_smulₛₗ, baseChangeValues_of_tmul, hpsi,
      correction_apply]
  have hincl : baseChangeInclusion p D D' M (c • m) =
      algebraMap D D' c • baseChangeInclusion p D D' M m :=
    (baseChangeInclusion p D D' M).map_smulₛₗ c m
  have hscalar : (c • b') • baseChangeValues p D D' M Omega Omega' psi (nabla m) =
      b' • (algebraMap D D' c • baseChangeValues p D D' M Omega Omega' psi (nabla m)) := by
    rw [Algebra.smul_def, ← mul_smul, mul_comm]
  rw [rawFormula, rawFormula, hform, hnabla, hincl, hscalar, correction_add_form,
    correction_smul_form, correction_smul_form, _root_.map_smul, smul_add]
  abel

/-- **The base-changed connection on the uncompleted tensor product** `D' ⊗[D] M`, with values in
the completion `M' ⊗̂_{D'} Ω'`.  It is additive and not `D'`-linear. -/
public noncomputable def rawBaseChange (hadd' : ∀ x y : D', d' (x + y) = d' x + d' y)
    (hleib' : ∀ x y : D', d' (x * y) = x • d' y + y • d' x)
    (hpsi : ∀ x : D, psi (d x) = d' (algebraMap D D' x)) :
    (D' ⊗[D] M) →+ CompletedTensor p D' Omega' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :=
  TensorProduct.liftAddHom
    (AddMonoidHom.mk'
      (fun b' => AddMonoidHom.mk' (rawFormula p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla b')
        (rawFormula_add_right p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla b'))
      (fun b c => AddMonoidHom.ext fun m =>
        rawFormula_add_left p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' b c m))
    (fun c b' m => rawFormula_balanced p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hleib' hpsi c b' m)

variable (hadd' : ∀ x y : D', d' (x + y) = d' x + d' y)
  (hleib' : ∀ x y : D', d' (x * y) = x • d' y + y • d' x)
  (hpsi : ∀ x : D, psi (d x) = d' (algebraMap D D' x))

/-- **The defining formula `∇' (b' ⊗ m) = b' · ψ_*(∇ m) + (1 ⊗ m) ⊗ d' b'`** on the uncompleted
tensor product. -/
public theorem rawBaseChange_tmul (b' : D') (m : M) :
    rawBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi (b' ⊗ₜ[D] m) =
      b' • baseChangeValues p D D' M Omega Omega' psi (nabla m) +
        correction p D D' M Omega' (d' b') (baseChangeInclusion p D D' M m) :=
  rfl

/-- **The Leibniz rule for the uncompleted base change**, with the correction term read on the
image of `D' ⊗[D] M` in the completion. -/
public theorem rawBaseChange_smul (b' : D') (a : D' ⊗[D] M) :
    rawBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi (b' • a) =
      b' • rawBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi a +
        correction p D D' M Omega' (d' b')
          (AdicCompletion.of (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) (D' ⊗[D] M) a) := by
  induction a using TensorProduct.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | tmul c m =>
    rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul', smul_eq_mul, rawBaseChange_tmul, rawBaseChange_tmul,
      of_tmul_eq_smul_inclusion, hleib' b' c, correction_add_form, correction_smul_form,
      correction_smul_form, _root_.map_smul, smul_add, mul_smul]
    abel
  | add x y hx hy =>
    rw [smul_add, _root_.map_add, hx, hy]
    simp only [_root_.map_add, smul_add]
    abel

/-! ### The base-changed connection on the completion -/

/-- The base-changed connection at the level `pⁿ`, the map induced by
`Crystalline.CompletedConnection.rawBaseChange` on the quotient by `(p)ⁿ`. -/
public noncomputable def levelBaseChange (n : ℕ) :
    (D' ⊗[D] M) ⧸ ((pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) ^ n • ⊤ : Submodule D' (D' ⊗[D] M)) →+
      (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M ⊗[D'] Omega') ⧸
        ((pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) ^ n • ⊤ :
          Submodule D' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M ⊗[D'] Omega')) :=
  QuotientAddGroup.lift _
    ((AdicCompletion.eval (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p)
        (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M ⊗[D'] Omega') n).toAddMonoidHom.comp
      (rawBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi))
    (fun _ hy ↦ CompletedDeRham.val_eq_zero_of_mem p D' _ n hy)

/-- The level-`pⁿ` base-changed connection on the class of an element is the level-`pⁿ`
component of the defining formula. -/
@[simp] public theorem levelBaseChange_mk (n : ℕ) (y : D' ⊗[D] M) :
    levelBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi n
        (Submodule.Quotient.mk y) =
      (rawBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi y).val n :=
  rfl

/-- **The base-changed connection `∇' : M' → M' ⊗̂_{D'} Ω'`**, as a function: at every level `pⁿ`
it is the formula `∇' (b' ⊗ m) = b' · ψ_*(∇ m) + (1 ⊗ m) ⊗ d' b'`. -/
public noncomputable def baseChangeFun (x : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :
    CompletedTensor p D' Omega' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :=
  ⟨fun n ↦ levelBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi n (x.val n), by
    intro m n hmn
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective
      ((pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) ^ n • ⊤ : Submodule D' (D' ⊗[D] M)) (x.val n)
    have hxm : x.val m = Submodule.Quotient.mk y := by
      rw [← x.property hmn, ← hy, CompletedDeRham.transitionMap_mk p D' hmn]
    change AdicCompletion.transitionMap (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p)
        (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M ⊗[D'] Omega') hmn
        (levelBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi n (x.val n)) =
      levelBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi m (x.val m)
    rw [hxm, ← hy, levelBaseChange_mk, levelBaseChange_mk]
    exact (rawBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi y).property hmn⟩

/-- The base-changed connection is computed level by level. -/
@[simp] public theorem baseChangeFun_val (n : ℕ) (x : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :
    (baseChangeFun p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi x).val n =
      levelBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi n (x.val n) :=
  rfl

/-- On the image of the uncompleted tensor product the base-changed connection is the defining
formula. -/
public theorem baseChangeFun_of (a : D' ⊗[D] M) :
    baseChangeFun p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi
        (AdicCompletion.of (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) (D' ⊗[D] M) a) =
      rawBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi a := by
  refine AdicCompletion.ext fun n ↦ ?_
  rw [baseChangeFun_val]
  rfl

/-- The base-changed connection is additive. -/
public theorem baseChangeFun_add (x y : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :
    baseChangeFun p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi (x + y) =
      baseChangeFun p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi x +
        baseChangeFun p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi y := by
  refine AdicCompletion.ext fun n ↦ ?_
  rw [baseChangeFun_val, AdicCompletion.val_add_apply, _root_.map_add,
    AdicCompletion.val_add_apply, baseChangeFun_val, baseChangeFun_val]

/-- **The Leibniz rule for the base-changed connection, with its correction term**, on the whole
of `M'`: `∇' (b' • x) = b' • ∇' x + x ⊗ d' b'`. -/
public theorem baseChangeFun_smul (b' : D') (x : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :
    baseChangeFun p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi (b' • x) =
      b' • baseChangeFun p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi x +
        toCompletedTensor p D' Omega' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) (x ⊗ₜ[D'] d' b') := by
  refine AdicCompletion.ext fun n ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ (x.val n)
  have hval : (b' • x).val n = Submodule.Quotient.mk (b' • a) := by
    rw [AdicCompletion.val_smul_apply, ← ha, Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul]
  have hofa : (AdicCompletion.of (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) (D' ⊗[D] M) a).val n = x.val n := by
    rw [AdicCompletion.of_apply, ← ha, Submodule.mkQ_apply]
  rw [baseChangeFun_val, hval, levelBaseChange_mk,
    rawBaseChange_smul p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi b' a,
    AdicCompletion.val_add_apply, AdicCompletion.val_add_apply,
    AdicCompletion.val_smul_apply, AdicCompletion.val_smul_apply,
    baseChangeFun_val, ← ha, levelBaseChange_mk,
    correction_val_congr p D D' M Omega' n (d' b') hofa, correction_apply]

/-- **The base-changed completed connection `∇' : M' → M' ⊗̂_{D'} Ω'`** of [Stacks, Tag 07JC].
Its Leibniz rule over `D'` is `∇' (b' • x) = b' • ∇' x + x ⊗ d' b'`. -/
public noncomputable def baseChange :
    CompletedConnection p D' Omega' d' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) where
  toFun := baseChangeFun p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi
  map_add' := baseChangeFun_add p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi
  leibniz' := baseChangeFun_smul p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi

/-- The base-changed connection of [Stacks, Tag 07JC] is computed level by level. -/
@[simp] public theorem baseChange_val (n : ℕ) (x : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :
    (baseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi x).val n =
      levelBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi n (x.val n) :=
  rfl

/-- **The defining formula `∇' (b' ⊗ m) = b' · ψ_*(∇ m) + (1 ⊗ m) ⊗ d' b'`** for the base-changed
connection, on the image of the uncompleted tensor product. -/
public theorem baseChange_of_tmul (b' : D') (m : M) :
    baseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi
        (AdicCompletion.of (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) (D' ⊗[D] M) (b' ⊗ₜ[D] m)) =
      b' • baseChangeValues p D D' M Omega Omega' psi (nabla m) +
        correction p D D' M Omega' (d' b') (baseChangeInclusion p D D' M m) := by
  change baseChangeFun p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi
      (AdicCompletion.of (pAdicIdeal (A := D') p) (D' ⊗[D] M) (b' ⊗ₜ[D] m)) = _
  rw [baseChangeFun_of, rawBaseChange_tmul]

/-- **The Leibniz rule of [Stacks, Tag 07JC] for the base-changed connection**:
`∇' (b' • x) = b' • ∇' x + x ⊗ d' b'`. -/
public theorem baseChange_smul (b' : D') (x : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :
    baseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi (b' • x) =
      b' • baseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi x +
        toCompletedTensor p D' Omega' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) (x ⊗ₜ[D'] d' b') :=
  (baseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi).leibniz b' x

/-- **Horizontality of the inclusion `m ↦ 1 ⊗ m`**: the base-changed connection applied to
`1 ⊗ m` is `ψ_*` applied to `∇ m`. -/
public theorem baseChange_inclusion (m : M) :
    baseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi
        (baseChangeInclusion p D D' M m) =
      baseChangeValues p D D' M Omega Omega' psi (nabla m) := by
  rw [baseChangeInclusion_apply, baseChange_of_tmul, one_smul,
    eq_zero_of_leibniz hleib', correction_apply, TensorProduct.tmul_zero, map_zero, add_zero]

/-- **The base-changed connection is determined by its defining formula at the levels**: any map
whose level-`n` value is computed from any representative of the level-`n` reduction by
`Crystalline.CompletedConnection.rawBaseChange` is the base-changed connection. -/
public theorem baseChange_eq_of_val
    (delta : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M →
      CompletedTensor p D' Omega' (baseChangeCarrier p D D' M))
    (h : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) (y : D' ⊗[D] M),
      x.val n = Submodule.Quotient.mk y →
        (delta x).val n =
          (rawBaseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi y).val n)
    (x : baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :
    delta x = baseChange p D D' M Omega Omega' d' psi nabla hadd' hleib' hpsi x := by
  refine AdicCompletion.ext fun n ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ (x.val n)
  rw [h n x y hy.symm, baseChange_val, ← hy, levelBaseChange_mk]

end BaseChange

end CompletedConnection

/-! ### The base-changed pair -/

namespace Pair

variable (p : ℕ) (D : Type u) [CommRing D] (D' : Type u') [CommRing D'] [Algebra D D']
  (Omega : Type v) [AddCommGroup Omega] [Module D Omega]
  (Omega' : Type v') [AddCommGroup Omega'] [Module D' Omega']
  {ι : Type uI} (dx : ι → Omega) {ι' : Type uI'} (dx' : ι' → Omega')
  {d : D → Omega} (d' : D' → Omega') (psi : Omega →ₛₗ[algebraMap D D'] Omega')

/-- **The base change of a pair along a divided power morphism `D → D'`**, the functor `F` of the
proof of [Stacks, Lemma 60.17.5, Tag 07L5].  The module is `M' = M ⊗̂_{D} D'` and the connection
is `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChange`. The existence of coordinate operators relative
to the family `dx'` (`hcoord`), integrability [Stacks, Tag 07JD] (`hint`) and topological
quasi-nilpotence [Stacks, Tag 07JE] (`hqn`) of `∇'` are hypotheses. -/
public noncomputable def baseChange (P : Pair.{u, v, uI, w} p D Omega dx d)
    (hadd' : ∀ x y : D', d' (x + y) = d' x + d' y)
    (hleib' : ∀ x y : D', d' (x * y) = x • d' y + y • d' x)
    (hpsi : ∀ x : D, psi (d x) = d' (algebraMap D D' x))
    (hcoord : ∃ theta : ι' →
        (CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' P.carrier →
          CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' P.carrier),
      IsCoordinateExpansion p D' Omega' dx'
        (CompletedConnection.baseChange p D D' P.carrier Omega Omega' d' psi P.nabla
          hadd' hleib' hpsi) theta)
    (hint : IsIntegrable p D' Omega' dx'
      (CompletedConnection.baseChange p D D' P.carrier Omega Omega' d' psi P.nabla
        hadd' hleib' hpsi))
    (hqn : IsTopologicallyQuasiNilpotent p D' Omega' dx'
      (CompletedConnection.baseChange p D D' P.carrier Omega Omega' d' psi P.nabla
        hadd' hleib' hpsi)) :
    Pair.{u', v', uI', max u' w} p D' Omega' dx' d' where
  carrier := CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' P.carrier
  isPAdicallyComplete :=
    CompletedConnection.isPAdicallyComplete_baseChangeCarrier p D D' P.carrier
  nabla := CompletedConnection.baseChange p D D' P.carrier Omega Omega' d' psi P.nabla
    hadd' hleib' hpsi
  hasCoordinateOperators := hcoord
  isIntegrable := hint
  isTopologicallyQuasiNilpotent := hqn

end Pair

/-- Mathlib's completion `AdicCompletion.map` of a linear map is the completion that
`Crystalline.adicCompletionMapₛₗ` builds from the same map read as semilinear over the identity
ring map. -/
theorem adicCompletionMap_eq_mapₛₗ {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {X Y : Type*} [AddCommGroup X]
    [Module R X] [AddCommGroup Y] [Module R Y] (I : Ideal R) (f : X →ₗ[R] Y)
    (x : AdicCompletion I X) :
    AdicCompletion.map I f x = adicCompletionMapₛₗ f (le_of_eq (Ideal.map_id I)) x := by
  refine AdicCompletion.ext fun n ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ (x.val n)
  change f.reduceModIdeal (I ^ n) (x.val n) =
    adicQuotientMap f (le_of_eq (Ideal.map_id I)) n (x.val n)
  rw [← ha]
  rfl

/-! ### The base change map of completed de Rham complexes -/

namespace CompletedDeRham

open CategoryTheory

section BaseChangeComplex

variable (p : ℕ) (D : Type u) [CommRing D] (D' : Type u) [CommRing D'] [Algebra D D']
  (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module D M]
  (Om : ℕ → Type u) [∀ i, AddCommGroup (Om i)] [∀ i, Module D (Om i)]
  (Om' : ℕ → Type u) [∀ i, AddCommGroup (Om' i)] [∀ i, Module D' (Om' i)]
  (psi : ∀ i, Om i →ₛₗ[algebraMap D D'] Om' i)
  (wedge : ∀ i, Om i →ₗ[D] Om 1 →ₗ[D] Om (i + 1))
  (wedge' : ∀ i, Om' i →ₗ[D'] Om' 1 →ₗ[D'] Om' (i + 1))
  (deRham : ∀ i, Om i →+ Om (i + 1)) (deRham' : ∀ i, Om' i →+ Om' (i + 1))
  {d : D → Om 1} (d' : D' → Om' 1) (nabla : CompletedConnection p D (Om 1) d M)
  (hd'add : ∀ x y : D', d' (x + y) = d' x + d' y)
  (hd'leib : ∀ x y : D', d' (x * y) = x • d' y + y • d' x)
  (hpsi1 : ∀ x : D, psi 1 (d x) = d' (algebraMap D D' x))
  (hleib : IsGradedLeibniz D Om wedge deRham d)
  (hleib' : IsGradedLeibniz D' Om' wedge' deRham' d')
  (hpsi_wedge : ∀ (i : ℕ) (omega : Om i) (eta : Om 1),
    psi (i + 1) (wedge i omega eta) = wedge' i (psi i omega) (psi 1 eta))
  (hpsi_deRham : ∀ (i : ℕ) (omega : Om i),
    psi (i + 1) (deRham i omega) = deRham' i (psi i omega))

/-- **The degree-`i` component of the base change map of completed de Rham complexes**: the
completed map `m ⊗ ω ↦ (1 ⊗ m) ⊗ ψ_i ω`, that is
`Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChangeValues` for the degree-`i` comparison of forms, read
as a map of abelian groups. -/
public noncomputable def baseChangeTerm (i : ℕ) :
    CompletedTensor p D (Om i) M →+
      CompletedTensor p D' (Om' i) (CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) :=
  (CompletedConnection.baseChangeValues p D D' M (Om i) (Om' i) (psi i)).toAddMonoidHom

/-- The degree-`i` component of the base change map on the image of an uncompleted pure tensor:
`m ⊗ ω ↦ (1 ⊗ m) ⊗ ψ_i ω`. -/
@[simp] public theorem baseChangeTerm_of_tmul (i : ℕ) (m : M) (omega : Om i) :
    baseChangeTerm p D D' M Om Om' psi i (toCompletedTensor p D (Om i) M (m ⊗ₜ[D] omega)) =
      toCompletedTensor p D' (Om' i) (CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' M)
        (CompletedConnection.baseChangeInclusion p D D' M m ⊗ₜ[D'] psi i omega) :=
  CompletedConnection.baseChangeValues_of_tmul p D D' M (Om i) (Om' i) (psi i) m omega

/-- The composite of left exterior multiplication by an `i`-form with the base change of an
uncompleted tensor product: the semilinear map `m ⊗ η ↦ (1 ⊗ m) ⊗ ψ_{i+1} (ω ∧ η)`. -/
private noncomputable def wedgeComposite (i : ℕ) (omega : Om i) :
    (M ⊗[D] Om 1) →ₛₗ[algebraMap D D']
      (CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' M ⊗[D'] Om' (i + 1)) :=
  (CompletedConnection.baseChangeTensor p D D' M (Om (i + 1)) (Om' (i + 1))
    (psi (i + 1))).comp (LinearMap.lTensor M (wedge i omega))

include hpsi_wedge in
/-- **Left exterior multiplication commutes with the base change of the values of a
connection**, given that the comparison is multiplicative,
`ψ_{i+1} (ω ∧ η) = ψ_i ω ∧ ψ_1 η`. -/
public theorem baseChangeValues_wedgeMap (i : ℕ) (omega : Om i)
    (z : CompletedTensor p D (Om 1) M) :
    CompletedConnection.baseChangeValues p D D' M (Om (i + 1)) (Om' (i + 1)) (psi (i + 1))
        (wedgeMap p D Om wedge M i omega z) =
      wedgeMap p D' Om' wedge' (CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) i (psi i omega)
        (CompletedConnection.baseChangeValues p D D' M (Om 1) (Om' 1) (psi 1) z) := by
  have hmap : (pAdicIdeal (A := D) p).map (algebraMap D D') ≤ pAdicIdeal (A := D') p :=
    CompletedConnection.pAdicIdeal_map_le p D D'
  have hcomp : ∀ y : M ⊗[D] Om 1,
      wedgeComposite p D D' M Om Om' psi wedge i omega y =
        LinearMap.lTensor (CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' M)
            (wedge' i (psi i omega))
          (CompletedConnection.baseChangeTensor p D D' M (Om 1) (Om' 1) (psi 1) y) := by
    intro y
    induction y using TensorProduct.induction_on with
    | zero => simp only [map_zero]
    | tmul m eta =>
      change CompletedConnection.baseChangeInclusion p D D' M m ⊗ₜ[D']
          psi (i + 1) (wedge i omega eta) =
        CompletedConnection.baseChangeInclusion p D D' M m ⊗ₜ[D']
          wedge' i (psi i omega) (psi 1 eta)
      rw [hpsi_wedge i omega eta]
    | add a b ha hb => simp only [map_add, ha, hb]
  rw [wedgeMap, wedgeMap, CompletedConnection.baseChangeValues,
    CompletedConnection.baseChangeValues]
  simp only [LinearMap.coe_restrictScalars, adicCompletionMap_eq_mapₛₗ]
  trans adicCompletionMapₛₗ (wedgeComposite p D D' M Om Om' psi wedge i omega) hmap z
  · exact (adicCompletionMapₛₗ_comp_apply (LinearMap.lTensor M (wedge i omega))
      (CompletedConnection.baseChangeTensor p D D' M (Om (i + 1)) (Om' (i + 1)) (psi (i + 1)))
      (wedgeComposite p D D' M Om Om' psi wedge i omega) (le_of_eq (Ideal.map_id _)) hmap hmap
      (fun _ ↦ rfl) z).symm
  · exact adicCompletionMapₛₗ_comp_apply
      (CompletedConnection.baseChangeTensor p D D' M (Om 1) (Om' 1) (psi 1))
      (LinearMap.lTensor (CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' M)
        (wedge' i (psi i omega)))
      (wedgeComposite p D D' M Om Om' psi wedge i omega) hmap (le_of_eq (Ideal.map_id _)) hmap
      hcomp z

include hpsi_wedge hpsi_deRham in
/-- **The chain-map square of the base change of completed de Rham complexes**: the degree-`i`
component commutes with the two de Rham differentials,
`∇' ∘ ψ_* = ψ_* ∘ ∇` on `M ⊗̂_D Ω^i_D`. -/
public theorem baseChangeTerm_comm (i : ℕ) :
    (differential p D' Om' wedge' deRham' (CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' M)
          (CompletedConnection.baseChange p D D' M (Om 1) (Om' 1) d' (psi 1) nabla hd'add
            hd'leib hpsi1) hleib' i).comp
        (baseChangeTerm p D D' M Om Om' psi i) =
      (baseChangeTerm p D D' M Om Om' psi (i + 1)).comp
        (differential p D Om wedge deRham M nabla hleib i) := by
  have key : ∀ y : M ⊗[D] Om i,
      rawDifferential p D' Om' wedge' deRham'
          (CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' M)
          (CompletedConnection.baseChange p D D' M (Om 1) (Om' 1) d' (psi 1) nabla hd'add
            hd'leib hpsi1) hleib' i
          (CompletedConnection.baseChangeTensor p D D' M (Om i) (Om' i) (psi i) y) =
        CompletedConnection.baseChangeValues p D D' M (Om (i + 1)) (Om' (i + 1)) (psi (i + 1))
          (rawDifferential p D Om wedge deRham M nabla hleib i y) := by
    intro y
    induction y using TensorProduct.induction_on with
    | zero => simp only [map_zero]
    | tmul m omega =>
      rw [CompletedConnection.baseChangeTensor, TensorProduct.map_tmul, rawDifferential_tmul,
        rawDifferential_tmul, map_add,
        baseChangeValues_wedgeMap p D D' M Om Om' psi wedge wedge' hpsi_wedge,
        CompletedConnection.baseChangeValues_of_tmul, hpsi_deRham i omega,
        CompletedConnection.baseChange_inclusion]
    | add a b ha hb => simp only [map_add, ha, hb]
  refine AddMonoidHom.ext fun x ↦ ?_
  refine AdicCompletion.ext fun n ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ (x.val n)
  have hBi : (baseChangeTerm p D D' M Om Om' psi i x).val n =
      Submodule.Quotient.mk
        (CompletedConnection.baseChangeTensor p D D' M (Om i) (Om' i) (psi i) y) := by
    change adicQuotientMap (CompletedConnection.baseChangeTensor p D D' M (Om i) (Om' i) (psi i))
      (CompletedConnection.pAdicIdeal_map_le p D D') n (x.val n) = _
    rw [← hy]
    rfl
  change levelDifferential p D' Om' wedge' deRham'
      (CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' M)
      (CompletedConnection.baseChange p D D' M (Om 1) (Om' 1) d' (psi 1) nabla hd'add hd'leib
        hpsi1) hleib' i n ((baseChangeTerm p D D' M Om Om' psi i x).val n) =
    adicQuotientMap
      (CompletedConnection.baseChangeTensor p D D' M (Om (i + 1)) (Om' (i + 1)) (psi (i + 1)))
      (CompletedConnection.pAdicIdeal_map_le p D D') n
      ((differential p D Om wedge deRham M nabla hleib i x).val n)
  rw [hBi, levelDifferential_mk, differential_val, ← hy, levelDifferential_mk]
  exact congrArg (fun w : CompletedTensor p D' (Om' (i + 1))
    (CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' M) ↦ w.val n) (key y)

include hpsi_wedge hpsi_deRham in
/-- **The base change map of completed de Rham complexes**
`M ⊗^∧_D Ω^*_D ⟶ M' ⊗^∧_{D'} Ω^*_{D'}`, the morphism of `CochainComplex AddCommGrpCat ℕ` whose
degree-`i` component is `Crystalline.CompletedDeRham.baseChangeTerm`.  Its target is the complex
of the base-changed pair: the module is `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier` and
the connection is `Crystalline.CompletedConnection.baseChange`, as in
`Crystalline.Pair.baseChange`. This is the map `α` of the proof of
[Stacks, Lemma 60.21.4, Tag 07LH]. -/
public noncomputable def baseChangeComplexHom
    (hsq : IsSquareZero p D Om wedge deRham M nabla hleib)
    (hsq' : IsSquareZero p D' Om' wedge' deRham'
      (CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' M)
      (CompletedConnection.baseChange p D D' M (Om 1) (Om' 1) d' (psi 1) nabla hd'add hd'leib
        hpsi1) hleib') :
    complex p D Om wedge deRham M nabla hleib hsq ⟶
      complex p D' Om' wedge' deRham' (CompletedConnection.baseChangeCarrier p D D' M)
        (CompletedConnection.baseChange p D D' M (Om 1) (Om' 1) d' (psi 1) nabla hd'add hd'leib
          hpsi1) hleib' hsq' :=
  CochainComplex.ofHom (fun i ↦ AddCommGrpCat.ofHom (baseChangeTerm p D D' M Om Om' psi i))
    (fun i ↦ by
      rw [complex_d, complex_d]
      exact AddCommGrpCat.ext fun x ↦ by
        exact DFunLike.congr_fun (baseChangeTerm_comm p D D' M Om Om' psi wedge wedge' deRham
          deRham' d' nabla hd'add hd'leib hpsi1 hleib hleib' hpsi_wedge hpsi_deRham i) x)

end BaseChangeComplex

end CompletedDeRham

end Crystalline

end
